WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Quesar. Private AI operations.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.400
Follow the boundaries, one idea at a time.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.500
ABI separates its pure AI core from storage I/O.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.700
MCP owns the store-facing completion persistence tail.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Vector primitives and accelerator contracts.

6
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.700
The durable store integrates snapshots, WAL recovery and HNSW search.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Recovery can report corruption or I/O failure. Durability has limits.

8
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.900
Audit blocks carry predecessor hashes.

9
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.700
The block hash covers time, sequence, profile and metadata.

10
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Strict verification recomputes content hashes. Link-only verification does not.

11
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.700
Abbey, Aviva and ABI are persona profiles with identity contracts.

12
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Keyword routing is a local path. Explicit leading names can select a profile.

13
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.100
The scoped audit matches thirteen case-insensitive phrase patterns.

14
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.100
Six principles contribute, including safety and privacy.

15
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.000
Harm outside those phrases can escape detection.

16
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:36.700
A distributed cognitive fabric is a longer-term vision.

17
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.300
Compatibility and delivery require separate qualification.

18
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:48.000
Treat the roadmap as a direction, with questions still open.

19
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.700
Begin with a defined project.

20
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Discuss the scope, inspect the sources, and agree on the evidence needed.
